    "summary": "Blanket (uldebe or munnyuure), composed of 9 narrow strips of hand-woven and hand-spun cotton of white and one shade of indigo. These are hand-sewn together along the selvedges. Each strip has the same weft pattern, which is formed either by alternating the white weft with blue indigo, or by the addition of a supplementary weft float forming patterns of squares or alternate horizontal and vertical lines. In the central area of the cloth nine pattern bands alternate with white bands. The warp ends form a long fringe.",
